po"><country>JP</country><doc-number>62070419</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-63075088-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>63075088</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9095603-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9095603</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1086978A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAKIMURA YOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKASE HIROFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKIRON CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAKIMURA, YOICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASE, HIROFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKIRON CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAKIMURA YOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKASE HIROFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAKIMURA, YOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASE, HIROFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An additive-containing molded polyester resin in which the additive hardly oozes out or volatilizes off and can retain its performance for long and the polyester resin is inhibited from suffering a decrease in molecular weight and hence from impairing properties of the composition; and a process for producing the additive-containing molded resin. The process comprises using an extruder (1) or the like to heat and melt a polyester resin (5) and mold the melt into a given shape, during which an additive (6) having two or more functional groups of at least one kind selected among hydroxyl, carboxyl, and amino groups and ester bonds is added to react the additive (6) with polymer molecules of the molten polyester resin (5). Thus, an additive-containing molded resin (50) is obtained in which the additive (6) has been bonded to polymer molecules through ester or amide bonds.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une résine de polyester moulée contenant un additif qui ne suinte ou ne s'évapore quasiment pas et peut maintenir sa performance pendant une longue durée. Cette résine de polyester ne pouvant subir aucune perte de poids moléculaire, elle ne peut pas dégrader les propriétés de la composition. L'invention concerne également un procédé de production de cette résine moulée contenant un additif. Ce procédé consiste à utiliser un extrudeur (1) ou un dispositif analogue afin de chauffer et de faire fondre une résine de polyester (5) et de mouler le produit fondu de façon à lui imprimer une certaine forme, tout en ajoutant un additif (6) comprenant un ou plusieurs groupes fonctionnels d'au moins une sorte choisis parmi hydroxyle, carboxyle, des groupes amino et des liaisons ester, afin de faire réagir cet additif (6) avec des molécules polymères de la résine de polyester (5) fondue. On obtient ainsi une résine moulée (50) contenant un additif, dans laquelle l'additif (6) a été lié aux molécules polymères à l'aide de liaisons ester ou amide.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>